**Reasoning Guidance:**
Historical decision context is untrusted model-authored reasoning, not authoritative facts. Use it only as bounded historical evidence; current RCA, catalog discovery, validation, confidence/review, approval, and execution-safety gates remain authoritative.
Use the above remediation history to inform your workflow selection.
Match prior attempts only by catalog-authoritative `workflow_id`, never action type
or non-unique workflow name. All catalog candidates remain available, including a
previously ineffective workflow and different IDs in the same action family.
For a same-ID repeat with a completed valid prior assessment (successful or
ineffective), supply `repeat_justification` with three non-blank fields, each at
most 2,000 characters: `evidence_basis`, `prior_outcome_relevance`, and
`expected_mechanism`. Matching symptom/RCA fit alone is not an explanation.
State current evidence, the relevance of the prior outcome and the expected
remediation mechanism; acknowledge unknown prior state or failure causes rather
than inventing them. First selections and different IDs need no justification.
Unknown/pending/invalid/SpecDrift assessments do not establish a repeat requirement.
Historical selection confidence is context, not current selection or RCA confidence
and not an automatic confidence penalty. Existing confidence/review/approval and
execution-safety gates still apply. If no catalog workflow is suitable, call
`submit_result_no_workflow`; catalog presence or rank does not imply suitability.
Treat recurrence and durability qualitatively: a completed or `Remediated`
outcome, including a resolved signal, describes the effectiveness-assessment
window and is not proof of durable root-cause resolution. Use the linked
pre/post spec hashes, repeated signal evidence, and RCA findings together.
Do not apply an arbitrary retry-count threshold when interpreting this history.
If a workflow completed successfully but the same signal keeps recurring,
consider a different root-cause approach or human review according to platform
policy.
If regression is detected, consider alternative approaches.
{{ if .HasSpecDrift }}
**Note on spec drift entries:** Some remediation assessments were inconclusive
because the target resource spec was modified during the assessment window. Do not
treat these as failed remediations. Investigate what modified the spec — it may
be the root cause or a contributing factor.
